{"id":"poor","name":"Poor","aliases":["Poor"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:poor","torrey:poor-the"],"groups":["Figurative","Kindness To","Instances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Poor","text":"The Mosaic legislation regarding the poor is specially important. (1.) They had the right of gleaning the fields (Lev. 19:9, 10; Deut. 24:19, 21). (2.) In the sabbatical year they were to have their share of the produce of the fields and the vineyards (Ex. 23:11; Lev. 25:6). (3.) In the year of jubilee they recovered their property (Lev. 25:25-30). (4.) Usury was forbidden, and the pledged raiment was to be returned before the sun went down (Ex. 22:25-27; Deut. 24:10-13). The rich were to be generous to the poor (Deut. 15:7-11). (5.) In the sabbatical and jubilee years the bond-servant was to go free (Deut. 15:12-15; Lev. 25:39-42, 47-54). (6.) Certain portions from the tithes were assigned to the poor (Deut. 14:28, 29; 26:12, 13). (7.) They shared in the feasts (Deut. 16:11, 14; Neh. 8:10). (8.) Wages were to be paid at the close of each day (Lev. 19:13). In the New Testament (Luke …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6041","lemma":"עָנִי","xlit":"ʻânîy","gloss":"depressed, in mind or circumstances","kjv":"afflicted, humble, lowly, needy","count":53,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H34","lemma":"אֶבְיוֹן","xlit":"ʼebyôwn","gloss":"destitute","kjv":"beggar, needy, poor","count":50,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H1800","lemma":"דַּל","xlit":"dal","gloss":"dangling","kjv":"lean, needy, poor, weaker","count":40,"share":0.11},{"strong":"G4434","lemma":"πτωχός","xlit":"ptōchós","gloss":"akin to G4422 and the alternate of G4098 )","kjv":"beggar, poor","count":23,"share":0.06},{"strong":"H7326","lemma":"רוּשׁ","xlit":"rûwsh","gloss":"to be destitute","kjv":"lack, needy, poor","count":19,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H3490","lemma":"יָתוֹם","xlit":"yâthôwm","gloss":"a bereaved person","kjv":"fatherless, orphan","count":18,"share":0.05}],"verses":["Exod.22.25","Lev.19.10","Lev.